<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caparra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1508</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caparra was the first Spanish settlement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, founded in 1508 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-ponce-de-leon">Juan Ponce de León</a> a few kilometres inland from San Juan Bay. It served as the seat of government in the first years of the conquest, but its marshy, unhealthy site and distance from the harbour led the settlers to move to the islet of San Juan around 1521. The ruins of Ponce de León's stone house are preserved as a historic site.</p></div>
